{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Ben porat Yosef.</b> Meaning: the land of Yosef is fruitful and multiplies like a tree by a spring of waters." "<b>Daughters tread upon the wall.</b> Meaning: so much does it grow its produce and fruits that they tread upon the daughters — upon the towns; בנות as a term for towns, as in 'and its daughters.' <b>Upon the wall.</b> It grows its fruits up to the edge of the wall — that is, there is no empty space where it does not grow fruits. From the Rav Rabbi David z\"l."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:29.746351814Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}